"      ELAS_COQUE donne les propriétés matériaux (membrane, flexion) dans le repère\n"
"      intrinsèque de la coque.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"  Material behavior %(k1)s is not available for this modeling type\n"
"\n"
"   Advice:\n"
"   * For ELAS_HYPER, change to a 2D or 3D solid modeling type.\n"
"   * For ELAS_GLRC, use modeling type DKTG\n"
"   * For ELAS_MEMBRANE, use modeling type MEMBRANE&GRILLE_MEMBRANE\n"
"   * To model anisotropic plate/shell behavior, use either\n"
"      ELAS_COQUE or ELAS_ORTH.\n"
"   * With ELAS_ORTH, do not forget to define DEFI_COMPOSITE\n"
"      You can also use transversely isotropic ELAS_ORTH with correctly defined material parameters\n"
"   * With ELAS_COQUE you do not need DEFI_COMPOSITE. But note:\n"
"      ELAS_COQUE gives the material properties (membrane, bending) in the intrinsic\n"
"      coordinate system of the shell.\n"

